author ai
group gui
note Looking at a definition without leaving the place you are reading. Hover an identifier in any code view - the document, the Source view, the peek panel, the tooltip or a graph node - and what the language's server knows about it (signature, type, docs) appears as a floating tooltip; ctrl-click or double-click goes to its definition, alt-click keeps the definition at the top of the References panel, which is brought into sight for it. The server is asked live on its language's thread, which stays for the session, and the answer shows a frame or more later. A code view never asks anything itself: it reads what the Model already knows (Queries) and pushes a Hover or Definition action, and apply sends the request. A definition inside the repo lands on the symbol, or on the line when it is inside one; one outside the repo is shown as a grid of its lines, read from disk and drawn on the server thread. A language with a grammar but no server falls back to the symbol of that name; prose files answer nothing.

